 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "Optics Advisor (contained-intelligence proposal node) ⊣ Module-Seating
 Governor (independent censor). Entity is an optical-module-batch (a
 manufactured lot of camera/optical modules of one spec, either a
 smartphone camera-module batch or an automotive ADAS optical/camera
 sensor-module batch). Six ops: :optical-module-batch/intake (directory
 patch normalize, phase-3 auto-eligible when clean, the only auto op in
 this domain) -> :optical-standard-rules/verify (per-product-class
 evidence checklist against opticsworks.facts's SMARTPHONE-CAMERA/
 AUTOMOTIVE-ADAS catalog, never auto) -> :end-of-line-quality/screen
 (optical-clarity/dust-ingress/dead-pixel defect screen, evaluated
 unconditionally, HARD hold if unresolved) -> :robotics/simulate-lens-
 seating-test (a REAL physics-2d time-stepped lens-barrel press-fit
 seating-test simulation deriving :sim-peak-seating-force-n from the
 actual simulated collision impulse, never auto) -> dual actuation,
 BOTH always escalate to a human and both HARD-hold on a fabricated
 spec-basis, incomplete evidence, a missing or independently
 out-of-tolerance (over- or under-pressed) seating-force simulation, an
 out-of-band focus-back-distance-deviation ground-truth recheck, an
 unresolved end-of-line defect, or a double actuation:
 :actuation/ship-optical-module-batch (dispatches onward to
 cloud-itonami-isic-2630 for smartphone camera modules or
 cloud-itonami-isic-2910/cloud-itonami-isic-2920 for automotive
 optical/ADAS sensor modules) and :actuation/issue-optical-certificate
 (Optical Module Test Certificate: resolution/MTF test report + safety
 compliance)."}
